---
export const title = 'Usage';
export const order = 100;
import DemoComponentCard from '../../../../components/DemoComponentCard.astro';

import dataSource from '../_data-source.json';
---

<style is:inline>
  .table-demo {
    width: 100%;
    height: 32rem;
  }
</style>

<p>
  Set <code>columns</code> and <code>data</code> as properties. The header stays in view while
  the rows scroll, and the whole header cell sorts its column. Number columns
  (<code>type: 'number'</code>) align to the end and use tabular figures.
</p>
<p>
  Pin a column with <code>fixed: 'start'</code> (or <code>true</code>) to keep it in view while
  the table scrolls sideways, or with <code>fixed: 'end'</code> for a row-actions column. A soft
  shadow appears on the pinned edge only while content is scrolled under it.
</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang='html'>
  <div class='table-demo'>
    <wc-table id='table-usage' key-field='_id' selection='multiple' label='People'>
      <wc-pagination slot='footer'></wc-pagination>
    </wc-table>
  </div>

  <script is:inline define:vars={{ dataSource }}>
    const $table = document.getElementById('table-usage');
    $table.columns = [
      { name: 'name', label: 'Name', width: 14, fixed: 'start' },
      { name: 'age', label: 'Age', width: 6, type: 'number' },
      {
        name: 'eyeColor',
        label: 'Eye color',
        width: 9,
        template: row => `<wc-tag size='sm' accent='${row.eyeColor}'>${row.eyeColor}</wc-tag>`,
      },
      { name: 'company', label: 'Company', width: 12 },
      { name: 'email', label: 'Email', width: 22 },
      { name: 'address', label: 'Address', width: 28 },
      {
        name: 'actions',
        label: '',
        width: 4,
        fixed: 'end',
        sortable: false,
        align: 'center',
        template: () =>
          `<wc-icon-button variant='text' color='secondary' aria-label='More actions'><wc-icon name='more_vert'></wc-icon></wc-icon-button>`,
      },
    ];
    $table.data = dataSource;
    $table.addEventListener('row-click', event => console.log('row-click', event.detail.record));
  </script>
</DemoComponentCard>

<p>
  The table is a single tab stop. Inside it, the arrow keys move between cells, <kbd>Home</kbd> and
  <kbd>End</kbd> jump to the ends of a row, <kbd>Space</kbd> selects the focused row,
  <kbd>Enter</kbd> fires <code>cell-click</code> and <code>row-click</code>, and
  <kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>C</kbd> copies the cell text. On a column header, <kbd>Enter</kbd> sorts,
  <kbd>Shift</kbd>+<kbd>Enter</kbd> adds a sort level and <kbd>Alt</kbd>+<kbd>Left</kbd> or
  <kbd>Alt</kbd>+<kbd>Right</kbd> moves a reorderable column. The grid always reports
  <code>aria-rowcount</code> and <code>aria-colcount</code>.
</p>
<p>
  A column <code>template</code> may return a Lit <code>TemplateResult</code> or a string. A string
  is inserted as HTML without escaping, so build it only from trusted values.
</p>
